A template with a subscription stays a `String`, but a supported backend can keep it live.

### Still a String

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count $Int = 0
    view = [: Count: [$(count)]]
]

`view` has type `String`. The compiler keeps extra metadata about the subscription.

### HTML-JS live fragment

In an HTML-JS project, a top-level runtime template with a subscription can rerender when the source changes.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    count $Int = 0

    [: [$(count)]]
]

### Not every sink is live

`io.line` does not accept subscription-bearing reactive templates. An `assert`
message may carry a reactive template, but reads it as one failure-edge snapshot
and does not establish a live sink. HTML-Wasm rejects reachable reactive runtime
features for now.
